# fsai-open: citation metadata
# Author: KEYUR SHAILESHKUMAR PATEL (ORCID https://orcid.org/0009-0008-5261-043X)
# Conducted independently; not an official Brunel University London project.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use fsai-open, please cite it as below."
title: "fsai-open: open, tested driverless software for the IMechE FS-AI ADS-DV"
type: software
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-11-18
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Open, tested driverless software for the IMechE FS-AI ADS-DV. Stage 1: a DBC-checked CAN codec, a ROS 2
  bridge with safety interlocks, a deterministic emulator of the VCU autonomous-system state machine and
  conformance and pitfall test suites. Stage 2: a driving stack (LiDAR-camera cone perception, EKF-SLAM with
  learned tyre slip, path and racing-line planning, latency-compensated control, every FS-AI 2026 event and
  inspection mission, sensor-loss EBS), seeded rule-conformant tracks, simulated sensors with trackside
  clutter, an outside referee, stress runs and real-time ROS 2 runs, all with SHA-256/Merkle provenance.
  Synthetic-validated only. Drafted with an AI assistant (Claude, Anthropic); all design decisions by the author.
keywords:
  - Formula Student AI
  - driverless
  - CAN bus
  - ROS 2
  - SLAM
  - autonomous racing
  - verification
  - reproducibility
  - open science
authors:
  - given-names: "KEYUR SHAILESHKUMAR"
    family-names: "PATEL"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0008-5261-043X"
    affiliation: "MSc Artificial Intelligence student, Department of Computer Science, Brunel University London, UK; Independent researcher"
